Having said that, let me say that I do disagree with Tim.

The irony, of course, is how pragmatic Tim is in most regards (crypto anarchy  is driven by technology instead of persons' convictions, beliefs, or choices), yet he has this puritanical attitude toward government employees and those somehow imputed to receive tax money. If it's really true that the underlying technology drives what the government and private individuals can do, why get all righteous about people who don't understand our ideas? 

Think of it as a game. The game we're playing now sucks. Libertarians think there is a better game immediately available. What's so terrible about playing the game as it is? What is inconsistent about playing the current game while at the same time working toward changing games?

The thing that amazes me about the IRS is how many people really do consent to the whole stinking mess. 



