Date: Sat, 9 Oct 93 23:45:37 -0400
From: Bill MacIntosh <wk01739@worldlink.com>
Subject: MOVIE: Demolition Man

Well, for a B grade SF movie, Demolition Man has a couple features of 
interest to this list; cryonics and freedom.  Granted the treatment of 
cryonics is pure Hollywood nonsense, but hey, at least it's used.

The freedom part I found a bit more surprising.  There's even a brief 
libertarian speech given by the leader of the "underground".  Above ground is  
"perfect order", you know, clean, non-violent, safe, and very controlled 
(i.e. boring/rigid).

The movie uses the comedy/violence formula ala Lethal Weapon.  I thought the 
comedy was much more entertaining.  One of my favorite scenes is where the 
future police are watching video of Stallone's career while they debate 
whether to "thaw him out."  He's walking away from a flaming ruin with a 
dirty 7-8 yr old girl in his arms.

Women Reporter:  (Sticking mike into Stallone's face)  How do you justify 
destroying a $5 million mall to save this girl when her ransom was only 
$25,000?

Little girl:  Hey!  Fuck you lady!

They play up Stallone's troubles "fitting in" and the female cop who's a late 
20th century buff, but doesn't quite get the expressions right.

Female cop:  We're going to blow this guy.

Stallone:  Away.  We're going to blow this guy away.

Female cop:  Whatever.

There are also assorted special F/X that are sometimes interesting.

